IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `poa-dates`

-- Powers of Attorney Act 2014 (Vic) -- the rules, seat-neutral where the text is, worded for the principal (the person
-- who makes the enduring power of attorney) where a question needs a seat.
--
-- Focus: enduring powers of attorney for a person whose injury may take away, or has taken away, their decision making
-- capacity, and for the family member who acts as their attorney: capacity (ss 3-5A), making the power (Part 3), when
-- it can be used (Part 4), how it ends (Part 5), the attorney's duties, conflict transactions, protection and
-- compensation (Part 6), VCAT's jurisdiction (Part 8) and the offences of s 135. Out: Part 2 (non-enduring powers),
-- Part 7 (supportive attorney appointments), Part 8 Division 7 (wills), Part 10 (transitional). Reasons in NOTES.md.
--
-- Conventions (rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05): JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words ("means",
-- "if", "only if", "unless", "may not ... unless", "must not ... unless", a flat negative, a period it fixes); NOTHING,
-- or a "not covered" constructor, where the text is silent or a grant is limited by its own wording and the case falls
-- outside it. Each such site is tagged NOTHING-kind and each case-by-case reading is a fork line in NOTES.md (F1-F14).
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Powers of
-- Attorney Act 2014, Version No. 007 (26 April 2021), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance
-- with the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Powers of Attorney Act 2014: the rules`

§§ `Part 1 -- definitions and decision making capacity`

-- s 4(1): "a person has capacity to make a decision as to a matter (decision making capacity) if the person is able to
-- (a) understand the information relevant to the decision and the effect of the decision; (b) retain that information
-- ...; (c) use or weigh that information ...; (d) communicate the decision and the person's views and needs". (2): "a
-- person is presumed to have decision making capacity unless there is evidence to the contrary". (3): understanding an
-- explanation given in a way appropriate to the person counts. (4)(c), (d): capacity is not to be assumed absent from
-- appearance, or merely because a decision is unwise; (e) a person has capacity "if it is possible for the person to
-- make a decision in the matter with practicable and appropriate support". (5): a decision with a high risk of being
-- seriously injurious may, with other factors, be evidence. s 5: the assessor "must take reasonable steps" to assess at
-- the best time and place. The limbs are judgments of whoever assesses: inputs. Fork F1 (as in the Guardianship and
-- Administration Act 2019 encoding): doubt resting only on appearance or an unwise decision is not "evidence to the
-- contrary".
DECLARE `Whether I have decision making capacity` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am presumed to have it, as there is no evidence to the contrary (s 4(2))`
    `yes: I can understand, retain, use or weigh, and communicate the decision, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 4(1), (3), (4)(e))`
    `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 4(1), (4)(a), (b))`

GIVEN `there is evidence to the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the doubt rests only on my appearance or an unwise decision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can understand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can retain` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can use or weigh` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I can communicate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I have decision making capacity`
`s 4 -- my decision making capacity` `there is evidence to the contrary` `the doubt rests only on my appearance or an unwise decision` `I can understand` `I can retain` `I can use or weigh` `I can communicate` MEANS
    IF (NOT `there is evidence to the contrary`) OR `the doubt rests only on my appearance or an unwise decision`
    THEN `yes: I am presumed to have it, as there is no evidence to the contrary (s 4(2))`
    ELSE IF `I can understand` AND `I can retain` AND `I can use or weigh` AND `I can communicate`
         THEN `yes: I can understand, retain, use or weigh, and communicate the decision, with any practicable and appropriate support (s 4(1), (3), (4)(e))`
         ELSE `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 4(1), (4)(a), (b))`

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Whether I have decision making capacity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer says I have capacity` `the answer` IF
    NOT (`the answer` EQUALS `no: I do not have it for this matter, though I may for others, and it may be temporary (s 4(1), (4)(a), (b))`)

-- s 3(1): "nearest relative means the relative first listed in the definition of relative who has attained the age of
-- 18 years, the elder or eldest of two or more relatives described in any paragraph being preferred". relative: "(a)
-- spouse or domestic partner; (b) child; (c) parent or step-parent; (d) sibling or step-sibling; (e) grandparent; (f)
-- grandchild; (g) uncle or aunt; (h) nephew or niece" (a sibling includes one adopted by a parent, s 3(3)). The list
-- has eight paragraphs, not the ten of the Guardianship and Administration Act 2019: a parent and a step-parent are one
-- paragraph here, so the elder of the two is preferred (finding 9).
DECLARE `My nearest relative` IS ONE OF
    `my spouse or domestic partner (s 3, relative (a))`
    `my eldest adult child (s 3, relative (b))`
    `my elder or eldest parent or step-parent (s 3, relative (c))`
    `my eldest adult sibling or step-sibling (s 3, relative (d))`
    `my eldest grandparent (s 3, relative (e))`
    `my eldest adult grandchild (s 3, relative (f))`
    `my eldest uncle or aunt (s 3, relative (g))`
    `my eldest adult nephew or niece (s 3, relative (h))`
    `I have no relative aged 18 or over, so no nearest relative`

GIVEN `a spouse or domestic partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult child` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult parent or step-parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult sibling or step-sibling` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult grandparent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult grandchild` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult uncle or aunt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult nephew or niece` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `My nearest relative`
`s 3 -- my nearest relative` `a spouse or domestic partner` `an adult child` `an adult parent or step-parent` `an adult sibling or step-sibling` `an adult grandparent` `an adult grandchild` `an adult uncle or aunt` `an adult nephew or niece` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a spouse or domestic partner` THEN `my spouse or domestic partner (s 3, relative (a))`
        IF `an adult child` THEN `my eldest adult child (s 3, relative (b))`
        IF `an adult parent or step-parent` THEN `my elder or eldest parent or step-parent (s 3, relative (c))`
        IF `an adult sibling or step-sibling` THEN `my eldest adult sibling or step-sibling (s 3, relative (d))`
        IF `an adult grandparent` THEN `my eldest grandparent (s 3, relative (e))`
        IF `an adult grandchild` THEN `my eldest adult grandchild (s 3, relative (f))`
        IF `an adult uncle or aunt` THEN `my eldest uncle or aunt (s 3, relative (g))`
        IF `an adult nephew or niece` THEN `my eldest adult nephew or niece (s 3, relative (h))`
        OTHERWISE `I have no relative aged 18 or over, so no nearest relative`

-- s 3(1): "care worker, for an individual, means a person who performs services for the care of the individual and
-- receives remuneration for those services from any source, but does not include (a) a person who receives a carer
-- payment or other benefit from the Commonwealth or a State or a Territory ... for providing home care for the
-- individual; or (b) a person who is a health provider". A "means" definition: outside it, FALSE. A family member paid
-- by the injured person's compensation for caring is a care worker; one on a government carer payment is not
-- (finding 7).
GIVEN `paid for caring for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `receives a government carer payment for caring for me at home` IS A BOOLEAN
      `is a health provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3 -- this person is my care worker` `paid for caring for me` `receives a government carer payment for caring for me at home` `is a health provider` IF
    `paid for caring for me`
    AND (NOT `receives a government carer payment for caring for me at home`)
    AND (NOT `is a health provider`)

-- s 3(1): financial matter "means any matter relating to the principal's financial or property affairs, and includes
-- any legal matter that relates to the financial or property affairs"; personal matter "means any matter relating to
-- the principal's personal or lifestyle affairs, and includes any legal matter that relates to [them], but does not
-- include any matter that relates to medical treatment or medical research procedures"; legal matter includes
-- "bringing or defending a legal proceeding ... including settling a claim before or after a legal proceeding ...
-- starts". Fork F4: a claim for damages or compensation for an injury, and receiving the money (financial matter
-- example (d), "receiving and recovering money payable to the principal"), is a financial matter.
DECLARE `Kind of matter` IS ONE OF
    `a financial matter (including a legal matter about my money or property, such as my injury claim)`
    `a personal matter (including a legal matter about my personal or lifestyle affairs)`
    `medical treatment or a medical research procedure`

-- s 22(2): "a person may confine what is authorised to be done by an attorney (a) to personal matters only; or (b) to
-- financial matters only; or (c) to matters specified in the instrument of appointment."
DECLARE `What my power covers` IS ONE OF
    `personal matters only`
    `financial matters only`
    `both personal and financial matters`
    `matters I specified, including this one`
    `matters I specified, not including this one`

GIVEN `the scope` IS A `What my power covers`
      `the matter` IS A `Kind of matter`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22(2) -- my power covers the matter` `the scope` `the matter` IF
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter` EQUALS `medical treatment or a medical research procedure` THEN FALSE
        IF `the scope` EQUALS `both personal and financial matters` THEN TRUE
        IF `the scope` EQUALS `matters I specified, including this one` THEN TRUE
        IF `the scope` EQUALS `personal matters only` THEN `the matter` EQUALS `a personal matter (including a legal matter about my personal or lifestyle affairs)`
        IF `the scope` EQUALS `financial matters only` THEN `the matter` EQUALS `a financial matter (including a legal matter about my money or property, such as my injury claim)`
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Part 3 -- making an enduring power of attorney`

-- s 23(1): "A person may not make an enduring power of attorney unless (a) the person is of or over 18 years of age;
-- and (b) the person has decision making capacity in relation to making the enduring power of attorney." (2):
-- understanding its effect includes understanding the conditions and instructions, when it commences, that the
-- attorney has the principal's powers once exercisable, that the principal may revoke it while capable, that it
-- continues after loss of capacity, and that without capacity the principal cannot oversee it. "Unless": JUST FALSE.
DECLARE `Whether I can make an enduring power of attorney` IS ONE OF
    `yes: I am 18 or over and have decision making capacity to make it (s 23(1))`
    `no: I am under 18 (s 23(1)(a))`
    `no: I do not have decision making capacity to make it (s 23(1)(b))`

GIVEN `my age` IS A NUMBER
      `my capacity` IS A `Whether I have decision making capacity`
GIVETH A `Whether I can make an enduring power of attorney`
`s 23 -- whether I can make an enduring power of attorney` `my age` `my capacity` MEANS
    IF `my age` LESS THAN 18
    THEN `no: I am under 18 (s 23(1)(a))`
    ELSE IF `the answer says I have capacity` `my capacity`
         THEN `yes: I am 18 or over and have decision making capacity to make it (s 23(1))`
         ELSE `no: I do not have decision making capacity to make it (s 23(1)(b))`

-- s 22(1): "a person may authorise an eligible attorney to do anything on behalf of the person that a person can
-- lawfully do by an attorney". s 26: "To avoid doubt, despite section 22, a principal ... is not able to authorise an
-- attorney ... to (a) make or revoke a will ...; (b) make or revoke an enduring power of attorney ...; (c) vote ...;
-- (d) consent to the entering into or dissolution of a marriage ... or of a sexual relationship ...; (e) make or give
-- effect to a decision (i) about the care and wellbeing of any child of the principal; or (ii) about the adoption of a
-- child under 18 ...; (f) enter into ... a surrogacy arrangement ...; (g) consent to ... a substitute parentage order
-- ...; (h) manage the estate of the principal on the death of the principal; or (i) consent to an unlawful act." A flat
-- "is not able": JUST FALSE. Medical treatment is outside "personal matter" (s 3): not covered by this Act (NOTHING-kind).
-- Whether anything else is something "a person can lawfully do by an attorney" is borrowed law: an input (fork F13).
DECLARE `Kind of power to give` IS ONE OF
    `running, settling or defending a legal claim for me, and receiving the money`
    `managing my money, property and compensation`
    `deciding where and with whom I live, and other personal matters`
    `medical treatment decisions`
    `making or revoking my will`
    `making or revoking an enduring power of attorney for me`
    `voting for me in an election or referendum`
    `consenting to my marriage or sexual relationship, or its dissolution`
    `decisions about the care and wellbeing of my child, or adopting my child`
    `a surrogacy arrangement or a substitute parentage order`
    `managing my estate after my death`
    `consenting to an unlawful act`
    `something else a person can lawfully do by an attorney`
    `something a person cannot lawfully do by an attorney`

DECLARE `Whether I can give this power` IS ONE OF
    `yes: a financial matter (ss 3, 22)`
    `yes: a personal matter (ss 3, 22)`
    `yes: anything a person can lawfully do by an attorney (s 22(1))`
    `no: s 26 says an enduring power of attorney cannot authorise it`
    `no: it is not something a person can lawfully do by an attorney (s 22(1))`
    `not covered: medical treatment is outside personal matters (s 3); see the Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016`

GIVEN `the power` IS A `Kind of power to give`
GIVETH A `Whether I can give this power`
`ss 22, 26 -- whether I can give this power` `the power` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the power` EQUALS `running, settling or defending a legal claim for me, and receiving the money` THEN `yes: a financial matter (ss 3, 22)`
        IF `the power` EQUALS `managing my money, property and compensation` THEN `yes: a financial matter (ss 3, 22)`
        IF `the power` EQUALS `deciding where and with whom I live, and other personal matters` THEN `yes: a personal matter (ss 3, 22)`
        IF `the power` EQUALS `medical treatment decisions` THEN `not covered: medical treatment is outside personal matters (s 3); see the Medical Treatment Planning and Decisions Act 2016` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF `the power` EQUALS `something else a person can lawfully do by an attorney` THEN `yes: anything a person can lawfully do by an attorney (s 22(1))`
        IF `the power` EQUALS `something a person cannot lawfully do by an attorney` THEN `no: it is not something a person can lawfully do by an attorney (s 22(1))`
        OTHERWISE `no: s 26 says an enduring power of attorney cannot authorise it`

-- s 28(1): "An individual is eligible to be appointed as an attorney ... if the individual is a person (a) who is of
-- or over 18 years of age; and (b) who is not an insolvent under administration; and (c) who, if the individual is to
-- be an attorney for financial matters (i) has not been convicted or found guilty of an offence involving dishonesty;
-- or (ii) if [so], has disclosed the conviction or finding of guilt to the principal and the disclosure ... has been
-- recorded in the enduring power of attorney; and (d) who is not a care worker, a health provider or an accommodation
-- provider for the principal." (2): "A trustee company is eligible to be appointed as an attorney for financial
-- matters ... if the company is not a company against which a proceeding for winding up has commenced." (3): "The
-- Public Advocate is eligible to be appointed as an attorney ... for personal matters." s 22(4) hands "eligible
-- attorney" to Division 3: under the ruling on delegated definitions, when no head holds, JUST FALSE. Fork F5: an
-- attorney for both personal and financial matters is "an attorney for financial matters" for (c).
DECLARE `Kind of attorney` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a trustee company`
    `the Public Advocate, as attorney`
    `another body corporate`

DECLARE `Matters the attorney is for` IS ONE OF
    `for personal matters only`
    `for financial matters only`
    `for both personal and financial matters`

GIVEN `the matters` IS A `Matters the attorney is for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the attorney is for financial matters` `the matters` IF
    NOT (`the matters` EQUALS `for personal matters only`)

GIVEN `the matters` IS A `Matters the attorney is for`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the attorney is for personal matters` `the matters` IF
    NOT (`the matters` EQUALS `for financial matters only`)

DECLARE `Whether this person is eligible to be my attorney` IS ONE OF
    `yes: an individual eligible under s 28(1)`
    `yes: a trustee company eligible for financial matters (s 28(2))`
    `yes: the Public Advocate is eligible for personal matters (s 28(3))`
    `no: under 18 (s 28(1)(a))`
    `no: an insolvent under administration (s 28(1)(b))`
    `no: convicted or found guilty of an offence involving dishonesty, not disclosed to me and recorded in the power (s 28(1)(c))`
    `no: my care worker, health provider or accommodation provider (s 28(1)(d))`
    `no: a trustee company against which a winding up proceeding has commenced (s 28(2))`
    `no: a trustee company may be attorney only for financial matters (ss 22(4), 28(2))`
    `no: the Public Advocate may be attorney only for personal matters (ss 22(4), 28(3))`
    `no: only an individual, a trustee company or the Public Advocate is eligible (ss 22(4), 28)`

GIVEN `the attorney` IS A `Kind of attorney`
      `the matters` IS A `Matters the attorney is for`
      `their age` IS A NUMBER
      `they are an insolvent under administration` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have a dishonesty conviction or finding of guilt` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was disclosed to me and recorded in the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are my care worker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are my health provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are my accommodation provider` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a winding up proceeding has commenced against the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether this person is eligible to be my attorney`
`s 28 -- whether this person is eligible to be my attorney` `the attorney` `the matters` `their age` `they are an insolvent under administration` `they have a dishonesty conviction or finding of guilt` `it was disclosed to me and recorded in the power` `they are my care worker` `they are my health provider` `they are my accommodation provider` `a winding up proceeding has commenced against the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the attorney`
    WHEN `an individual` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `their age` LESS THAN 18 THEN `no: under 18 (s 28(1)(a))`
            IF `they are an insolvent under administration` THEN `no: an insolvent under administration (s 28(1)(b))`
            IF (`the attorney is for financial matters` `the matters`) AND `they have a dishonesty conviction or finding of guilt` AND (NOT `it was disclosed to me and recorded in the power`)
                THEN `no: convicted or found guilty of an offence involving dishonesty, not disclosed to me and recorded in the power (s 28(1)(c))`
            IF `they are my care worker` OR `they are my health provider` OR `they are my accommodation provider`
                THEN `no: my care worker, health provider or accommodation provider (s 28(1)(d))`
            OTHERWISE `yes: an individual eligible under s 28(1)`
    WHEN `a trustee company` THEN
        IF `the attorney is for personal matters` `the matters`
        THEN `no: a trustee company may be attorney only for financial matters (ss 22(4), 28(2))`
        ELSE IF `a winding up proceeding has commenced against the company`
             THEN `no: a trustee company against which a winding up proceeding has commenced (s 28(2))`
             ELSE `yes: a trustee company eligible for financial matters (s 28(2))`
    WHEN `the Public Advocate, as attorney` THEN
        IF `the attorney is for financial matters` `the matters`
        THEN `no: the Public Advocate may be attorney only for personal matters (ss 22(4), 28(3))`
        ELSE `yes: the Public Advocate is eligible for personal matters (s 28(3))`
    OTHERWISE `no: only an individual, a trustee company or the Public Advocate is eligible (ss 22(4), 28)`

-- s 30(3)(b): if the principal "does not specify how the attorneys are appointed, the attorneys are taken to be
-- appointed to act as joint attorneys". (4): "Unless an enduring power of attorney otherwise provides", joint attorneys
-- act unanimously, several attorneys "as one alone", joint and several attorneys either way, majority attorneys by a
-- majority; a document is signed by those who act. Where the power provides otherwise, the answer says so.
DECLARE `How my attorneys were appointed` IS ONE OF
    `jointly`
    `severally`
    `jointly and severally`
    `by majority`
    `I did not say`

DECLARE `How my attorneys must act` IS ONE OF
    `all of them together, all signing (s 30(3)(b), (4)(a))`
    `any one alone, signing alone (s 30(4)(b))`
    `all together, or any one or more of them alone, those acting signing (s 30(4)(c))`
    `a majority agreeing, the majority signing (s 30(4)(d))`
    `as the power itself provides (s 30(4))`

GIVEN `the appointment` IS A `How my attorneys were appointed`
      `the power provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `How my attorneys must act`
`s 30 -- how my attorneys must act` `the appointment` `the power provides otherwise` MEANS
    IF `the power provides otherwise`
    THEN `as the power itself provides (s 30(4))`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the appointment`
         WHEN `severally` THEN `any one alone, signing alone (s 30(4)(b))`
         WHEN `jointly and severally` THEN `all together, or any one or more of them alone, those acting signing (s 30(4)(c))`
         WHEN `by majority` THEN `a majority agreeing, the majority signing (s 30(4)(d))`
         OTHERWISE `all of them together, all signing (s 30(3)(b), (4)(a))`

-- ss 32, 33, 34, 35, 36, 5A (and their twins for an instrument of revocation, ss 45, 46, 47, 48, 49). The instrument
-- "must be in the prescribed form" (s 32, s 45) and "must be executed (a) by (i) the principal signing ...; or (ii) a
-- person, who is eligible to do so under section 34, signing ... in the presence of and at the direction of the
-- principal; and (b) by 2 persons (i) who are present and who witness the signing ...; and (ii) who sign and date the
-- instrument in the presence of the principal and in the presence of each other; and (iii) who certify in writing ...
-- in the manner required by section 36." s 34 (s 47): the signer is "of or over the age of 18 years", "not a witness"
-- and "not an attorney". s 35 (s 48): "(1)(a) both persons must be eligible ...; (b) one person must be either
-- authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner"; "(2) ... eligible ... if the person (a) is of or over
-- the age of 18 years; and (b) is not signing the instrument at the direction of the principal; and (c) is not an
-- attorney ...; and (d) is not (i) a relative of the principal; or (ii) a relative of an attorney ...; or (iii) a care
-- worker or an accommodation provider for the principal." s 5A: the remote witnessing procedure may be used (s 33(2),
-- s 46(2)); "(2) One of the witnesses must be a special witness", "(3) All elements ... must be carried out on the same
-- day and within Victoria", "(6) ... the special witness must sign the document last" and (7)(d) certify. An
-- instrument not executed as required is not valid unless VCAT decides it is (ss 116(1)(b), 117).
DECLARE `Kind of instrument` IS ONE OF
    `an enduring power of attorney`
    `an instrument of revocation`

GIVEN `their age` IS A NUMBER
      `they are an attorney or the person who signed for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are a relative of mine or of an attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are my care worker or accommodation provider` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 35(2), 48(2) -- the witness is eligible` `their age` `they are an attorney or the person who signed for me` `they are a relative of mine or of an attorney` `they are my care worker or accommodation provider` IF
    `their age` AT LEAST 18
    AND (NOT `they are an attorney or the person who signed for me`)
    AND (NOT `they are a relative of mine or of an attorney`)
    AND (NOT `they are my care worker or accommodation provider`)

GIVEN `their age` IS A NUMBER
      `they are a witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are an attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 34, 47 -- the person signing for me is eligible` `their age` `they are a witness` `they are an attorney` IF
    `their age` AT LEAST 18 AND (NOT `they are a witness`) AND (NOT `they are an attorney`)

DECLARE `Whether the instrument was executed as the Act requires` IS ONE OF
    `yes: executed as the Act requires`
    `no: not in the prescribed form (s 32 or s 45)`
    `no: the person who signed for me was not eligible to (s 34 or s 47)`
    `no: a witness was not eligible (s 35(2) or s 48(2))`
    `no: neither witness is authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner (s 35(1)(b) or s 48(1)(b))`
    `no: the witnesses did not both witness the signing and sign and date it in my presence and each other's (s 33(1)(b) or s 46(1)(b))`
    `no: the witnesses did not certify and state as s 36 or s 49 requires`
    `no: the remote witnessing procedure was not followed (s 5A)`

GIVEN `the instrument` IS A `Kind of instrument`
      `it is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I signed it myself` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the signer for me is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the first witness is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the second witness is eligible` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a witness is authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both witnessed, signed and dated in my presence and each other's` IS A BOOLEAN
      `both certified and stated as required` IS A BOOLEAN
      `remote witnessing was used` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all on the same day and within Victoria` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a special witness signed last and certified the procedure` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether the instrument was executed as the Act requires`
`ss 32-36, 45-49, 5A -- whether the instrument was executed as the Act requires` `the instrument` `it is in the prescribed form` `I signed it myself` `the signer for me is eligible` `the first witness is eligible` `the second witness is eligible` `a witness is authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner` `both witnessed, signed and dated in my presence and each other's` `both certified and stated as required` `remote witnessing was used` `all on the same day and within Victoria` `a special witness signed last and certified the procedure` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `it is in the prescribed form` THEN `no: not in the prescribed form (s 32 or s 45)`
        IF (NOT `I signed it myself`) AND (NOT `the signer for me is eligible`) THEN `no: the person who signed for me was not eligible to (s 34 or s 47)`
        IF (NOT `the first witness is eligible`) OR (NOT `the second witness is eligible`) THEN `no: a witness was not eligible (s 35(2) or s 48(2))`
        IF NOT `a witness is authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner` THEN `no: neither witness is authorised to witness affidavits or a medical practitioner (s 35(1)(b) or s 48(1)(b))`
        IF NOT `both witnessed, signed and dated in my presence and each other's` THEN `no: the witnesses did not both witness the signing and sign and date it in my presence and each other's (s 33(1)(b) or s 46(1)(b))`
        IF NOT `both certified and stated as required` THEN `no: the witnesses did not certify and state as s 36 or s 49 requires`
        IF `remote witnessing was used` AND ((NOT `all on the same day and within Victoria`) OR (NOT `a special witness signed last and certified the procedure`)) THEN `no: the remote witnessing procedure was not followed (s 5A)`
        OTHERWISE `yes: executed as the Act requires`

-- s 37(1): the power "is effective as to an attorney ... if (a) ... the attorney signs a statement of acceptance ...
-- in the prescribed form; and (b) in the case of an attorney who is not a trustee company, a person of or over 18 years
-- of age witnesses the signing ... and signs that he or she has witnessed the signing; and (c) in the statement of
-- acceptance, the attorney states that the attorney (i) is eligible ...; (ii) understands the obligations ... and the
-- consequences of failing to comply ...; and (iii) undertakes to act in accordance with" the Act. s 38(1) adds for an
-- alternative attorney (iv) understands when they may act and (v) is prepared to act in the attorney's place. "If":
-- JUST FALSE when a limb fails.
GIVEN `they are an alternative attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are a trustee company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they signed a statement of acceptance in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an adult witnessed their signing and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says they are eligible, understand the obligations and undertake to comply` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement says they understand when they may act and are prepared to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 37, 38 -- my power is effective as to this attorney` `they are an alternative attorney` `they are a trustee company` `they signed a statement of acceptance in the prescribed form` `an adult witnessed their signing and signed` `the statement says they are eligible, understand the obligations and undertake to comply` `the statement says they understand when they may act and are prepared to act` IF
    `they signed a statement of acceptance in the prescribed form`
    AND (`they are a trustee company` OR `an adult witnessed their signing and signed`)
    AND `the statement says they are eligible, understand the obligations and undertake to comply`
    AND ((NOT `they are an alternative attorney`) OR `the statement says they understand when they may act and are prepared to act`)

§§ `Part 4 -- when my attorney may act, and s 83`

-- s 39(1): the principal may specify when the power is exercisable: "(a) immediately on the making of the power; or
-- (b) when the principal ceases to have decision making capacity for the matters or matter; or (c) any other time,
-- circumstance or occasion." (2): if nothing is specified, "exercisable on and from the making". (3): "Despite a
-- specification ..., if before the specified time, circumstance or occasion for a matter, the principal does not have
-- decision making capacity for the matter, an attorney ... may exercise that power during any period when the principal
-- does not have that capacity." s 41(1): an attorney who "has commenced exercising power ... because the principal does
-- not have decision making capacity ... may continue to exercise that power even if the principal regains" it. s 42:
-- the principal keeps their own power to act. s 83(1): if VCAT makes an administration order for the principal, the
-- attorney "must not exercise a power for financial matters ... unless ... authorised by VCAT ... and then only so far
-- as is authorised"; (2) the same for a guardianship order and personal matters. Whether the power is still in force
-- (Part 5) is a separate question.
DECLARE `When I said my power begins` IS ONE OF
    `nothing specified`
    `immediately`
    `when I cease to have decision making capacity for the matter`
    `another time, circumstance or occasion`

DECLARE `Whether my attorney may act now` IS ONE OF
    `yes: from the making of the power (s 39(1)(a), (2))`
    `yes: the time, circumstance or occasion I specified has come (s 39(1)(c))`
    `yes: while I do not have decision making capacity for the matter (s 39(1)(b), (3))`
    `yes: having begun to act because I lacked capacity, my attorney may continue though I have regained it (s 41)`
    `yes, but only so far as VCAT has authorised, as VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order (s 83)`
    `no: not yet; the time I specified has not come and I have capacity for the matter (s 39)`
    `no: VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order covering the matter and has not authorised my attorney (s 83)`
    `no: my power does not cover this matter (s 22(2))`
    `not covered: medical treatment is outside an enduring power of attorney (s 3)`

GIVEN `the scope` IS A `What my power covers`
      `the matter` IS A `Kind of matter`
      `the start` IS A `When I said my power begins`
      `the specified time has come` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I now lack decision making capacity for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my attorney began acting because I lacked capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has made an administration order for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has made a guardianship order for me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has authorised my attorney to act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may act now`
`ss 22, 39, 41, 83 -- whether my attorney may act now` `the scope` `the matter` `the start` `the specified time has come` `I now lack decision making capacity for the matter` `my attorney began acting because I lacked capacity` `VCAT has made an administration order for me` `VCAT has made a guardianship order for me` `VCAT has authorised my attorney to act` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the matter` EQUALS `medical treatment or a medical research procedure`
            THEN `not covered: medical treatment is outside an enduring power of attorney (s 3)` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF NOT (`s 22(2) -- my power covers the matter` `the scope` `the matter`)
            THEN `no: my power does not cover this matter (s 22(2))`
        IF `an order covers the matter` AND (NOT `VCAT has authorised my attorney to act`)
            THEN `no: VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order covering the matter and has not authorised my attorney (s 83)`
        IF `an order covers the matter` AND (`the answer lets my attorney act` `the answer under ss 39 and 41`)
            THEN `yes, but only so far as VCAT has authorised, as VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order (s 83)`
        OTHERWISE `the answer under ss 39 and 41`
    WHERE
        `the answer under ss 39 and 41` MEANS
            BRANCH
                IF `the start` EQUALS `nothing specified` OR `the start` EQUALS `immediately`
                    THEN `yes: from the making of the power (s 39(1)(a), (2))`
                IF `the start` EQUALS `another time, circumstance or occasion` AND `the specified time has come`
                    THEN `yes: the time, circumstance or occasion I specified has come (s 39(1)(c))`
                IF `I now lack decision making capacity for the matter`
                    THEN `yes: while I do not have decision making capacity for the matter (s 39(1)(b), (3))`
                IF `my attorney began acting because I lacked capacity`
                    THEN `yes: having begun to act because I lacked capacity, my attorney may continue though I have regained it (s 41)`
                OTHERWISE `no: not yet; the time I specified has not come and I have capacity for the matter (s 39)`
        `an order covers the matter` MEANS
            (`VCAT has made an administration order for me` AND `the matter` EQUALS `a financial matter (including a legal matter about my money or property, such as my injury claim)`)
            OR (`VCAT has made a guardianship order for me` AND `the matter` EQUALS `a personal matter (including a legal matter about my personal or lifestyle affairs)`)

GIVEN `the answer` IS A `Whether my attorney may act now`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the answer lets my attorney act` `the answer` IF
    `the answer` EQUALS `yes: from the making of the power (s 39(1)(a), (2))`
    OR `the answer` EQUALS `yes: the time, circumstance or occasion I specified has come (s 39(1)(c))`
    OR `the answer` EQUALS `yes: while I do not have decision making capacity for the matter (s 39(1)(b), (3))`
    OR `the answer` EQUALS `yes: having begun to act because I lacked capacity, my attorney may continue though I have regained it (s 41)`
    OR `the answer` EQUALS `yes, but only so far as VCAT has authorised, as VCAT has made an administration or guardianship order (s 83)`

-- s 31(2): an alternative attorney "is authorised to act ... (a) in the circumstances specified in the power of
-- attorney; or (b) if no circumstances are specified ... (i) if the attorney for whom the alternative attorney is
-- appointed (A) dies; or (B) does not have the decision making capacity for the matters ...; or (C) is otherwise not
-- willing or able to act; or (ii) if the appointment of the attorney ... is revoked by the operation of section 54."
-- "If": JUST FALSE when no limb holds. Fork F6: where circumstances are specified, (b)'s list does not also apply.
GIVEN `circumstances are specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the specified circumstances have arisen` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney lacks capacity for the matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney is not willing or able to act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney's appointment was revoked under s 54` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 31(2) -- my alternative attorney may act` `circumstances are specified` `the specified circumstances have arisen` `the attorney has died` `the attorney lacks capacity for the matters` `the attorney is not willing or able to act` `the attorney's appointment was revoked under s 54` IF
    IF `circumstances are specified`
    THEN `the specified circumstances have arisen`
    ELSE `the attorney has died` OR `the attorney lacks capacity for the matters` OR `the attorney is not willing or able to act` OR `the attorney's appointment was revoked under s 54`

§§ `Part 5 -- how my power, or an attorney's part of it, ends`

-- s 43: "revoked according to its terms". s 44: revocation by the principal (the instrument's validity is the
-- execution question). s 51: "revoked on the death of the principal". s 52: on the attorney's death, "revoked so far as
-- it gives power to that attorney". s 53: the same if the attorney loses decision making capacity for the matters.
-- s 54(1): for an individual attorney, if after appointment "(a) the attorney becomes an insolvent under
-- administration; or (b) ... becomes a care worker, a health provider or an accommodation provider for the principal;
-- or (c) for an attorney for financial matters, the attorney is convicted or found guilty of an offence involving
-- dishonesty"; (2) a trustee company "wound up or ceases to be registered". s 55: "revoked by a later enduring power of
-- attorney of the principal" unless the later one says otherwise. ss 56, 59: on resignation, revoked as to that
-- attorney. s 119: a declaration of invalidity makes it "void from its commencement". s 120(1): VCAT may revoke all or
-- part, revoke an attorney's appointment, or suspend. Each is a flat statement; the first that holds is answered.
DECLARE `Whether my power is in force as to this attorney` IS ONE OF
    `yes: nothing in Part 5 or Part 8 has ended it as to this attorney`
    `no: it is revoked according to its terms (s 43)`
    `no: it is revoked by my death (s 51)`
    `no: VCAT has declared it invalid; it is void from its commencement (s 119)`
    `no: I revoked it, or this attorney's appointment (s 44)`
    `no: revoked by my later enduring power of attorney (s 55)`
    `no: VCAT revoked it, or this attorney's appointment (s 120(1)(a), (b))`
    `no: revoked as to this attorney, who has died (s 52)`
    `no: revoked as to this attorney, who has lost decision making capacity for the matters (s 53)`
    `no: revoked as to this attorney, who became insolvent, my care worker, health provider or accommodation provider, or (for financial matters) was convicted of dishonesty, after appointment (s 54(1))`
    `no: revoked as to this trustee company, which was wound up or ceased to be registered (s 54(2))`
    `no: revoked as to this attorney, who resigned (ss 56, 59)`
    `suspended by VCAT for a specified period (s 120(1)(d))`

GIVEN `revoked by its terms` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT declared it invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I revoked it or this appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I made a later enduring power that does not keep this one` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT revoked it or this appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney lacks capacity for the matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an individual attorney became disqualified after appointment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a trustee company attorney was wound up or deregistered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the attorney resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT has suspended it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my power is in force as to this attorney`
`Part 5 -- whether my power is in force as to this attorney` `revoked by its terms` `I have died` `VCAT declared it invalid` `I revoked it or this appointment` `I made a later enduring power that does not keep this one` `VCAT revoked it or this appointment` `the attorney has died` `the attorney lacks capacity for the matters` `an individual attorney became disqualified after appointment` `a trustee company attorney was wound up or deregistered` `the attorney resigned` `VCAT has suspended it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `VCAT declared it invalid` THEN `no: VCAT has declared it invalid; it is void from its commencement (s 119)`
        IF `I have died` THEN `no: it is revoked by my death (s 51)`
        IF `revoked by its terms` THEN `no: it is revoked according to its terms (s 43)`
        IF `I revoked it or this appointment` THEN `no: I revoked it, or this attorney's appointment (s 44)`
        IF `I made a later enduring power that does not keep this one` THEN `no: revoked by my later enduring power of attorney (s 55)`
        IF `VCAT revoked it or this appointment` THEN `no: VCAT revoked it, or this attorney's appointment (s 120(1)(a), (b))`
        IF `the attorney has died` THEN `no: revoked as to this attorney, who has died (s 52)`
        IF `the attorney lacks capacity for the matters` THEN `no: revoked as to this attorney, who has lost decision making capacity for the matters (s 53)`
        IF `an individual attorney became disqualified after appointment` THEN `no: revoked as to this attorney, who became insolvent, my care worker, health provider or accommodation provider, or (for financial matters) was convicted of dishonesty, after appointment (s 54(1))`
        IF `a trustee company attorney was wound up or deregistered` THEN `no: revoked as to this trustee company, which was wound up or ceased to be registered (s 54(2))`
        IF `the attorney resigned` THEN `no: revoked as to this attorney, who resigned (ss 56, 59)`
        IF `VCAT has suspended it` THEN `suspended by VCAT for a specified period (s 120(1)(d))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: nothing in Part 5 or Part 8 has ended it as to this attorney`

-- s 44: the principal "may revoke the enduring power of attorney or the appointment of an attorney ... if the
-- principal has decision making capacity in relation to making an enduring power of attorney giving the same power".
-- s 45: by instrument in the prescribed form; ss 46-49 its execution; s 50: tell the attorneys (failure does not
-- affect validity). "If": JUST FALSE without that capacity.
GIVEN `my capacity to make the same power` IS A `Whether I have decision making capacity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 44 -- I may revoke my power` `my capacity to make the same power` IF
    `the answer says I have capacity` `my capacity to make the same power`

-- ss 56, 59: resignation. s 56(1): an attorney or alternative attorney "may resign ... at any time when the principal
-- has decision making capacity for the matter". s 59(1): when the principal does not, an attorney may resign "(a) if
-- there is another attorney who has power for the matter; or (b) if there is no other attorney ... but there is an
-- alternative attorney who has power for the matter who is able and willing to act; or (c) if paragraph (a) or (b) does
-- not apply, with leave from VCAT or the Supreme Court." (2): an alternative attorney who is acting, "with leave"; (3)
-- one who is not acting may resign. Forms: ss 57, 60; notices: ss 58, 61 (failure does not affect validity).
DECLARE `Whether the attorney may resign now` IS ONE OF
    `yes: at any time while the principal has capacity for the matter, in the prescribed form, telling the principal and the other attorneys (ss 56-58)`
    `yes: there is another attorney with power for the matter; in the prescribed form, telling the other attorneys and alternative attorneys (ss 59(1)(a), 60, 61(1))`
    `yes: an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing to act; in the prescribed form, telling the alternative attorneys (ss 59(1)(b), 60, 61(2))`
    `yes: an alternative attorney who is not acting may resign; in the prescribed form, telling the attorneys and other alternative attorneys (ss 59(3), 60, 61(3))`
    `only with leave from VCAT or the Supreme Court (s 59(1)(c) or (2))`

GIVEN `I am an alternative attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am acting as attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal has capacity for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another attorney has power for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether the attorney may resign now`
`ss 56, 59 -- whether the attorney may resign now` `I am an alternative attorney` `I am acting as attorney` `the principal has capacity for the matter` `another attorney has power for the matter` `an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the principal has capacity for the matter`
            THEN `yes: at any time while the principal has capacity for the matter, in the prescribed form, telling the principal and the other attorneys (ss 56-58)`
        IF `I am an alternative attorney`
            THEN IF `I am acting as attorney`
                 THEN `only with leave from VCAT or the Supreme Court (s 59(1)(c) or (2))`
                 ELSE `yes: an alternative attorney who is not acting may resign; in the prescribed form, telling the attorneys and other alternative attorneys (ss 59(3), 60, 61(3))`
        IF `another attorney has power for the matter`
            THEN `yes: there is another attorney with power for the matter; in the prescribed form, telling the other attorneys and alternative attorneys (ss 59(1)(a), 60, 61(1))`
        IF `an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing`
            THEN `yes: an alternative attorney with power for the matter is able and willing to act; in the prescribed form, telling the alternative attorneys (ss 59(1)(b), 60, 61(2))`
        OTHERWISE `only with leave from VCAT or the Supreme Court (s 59(1)(c) or (2))`

-- s 54(3): the attorney "must take reasonable steps to give notice in accordance with subsection (4) (a) if the
-- appointment ... is revoked by the operation of subsection (1) or (2); or (b) in the case of ... a trustee company, if
-- (i) a proceeding against the company for winding up commences; or (ii) the company is convicted or found guilty of an
-- offence involving dishonesty." (4): to "(a) the principal, if the principal has decision making capacity for the
-- matter ...; (b) any other attorney; (c) any alternative attorney; (d) if the principal does not have decision making
-- capacity ... and there is no person to notify under (b) or (c) (i) the nearest relative ...; or (ii) if the attorney
-- is not able to notify the nearest relative, the Public Advocate." (5) prescribed form; (6) failure does not affect
-- the revocation. With no event, s 54(3) asks nothing: an empty list.
DECLARE `Who must be told` IS ONE OF
    `the principal`
    `every other attorney`
    `every alternative attorney`
    `the principal's nearest relative`
    `the Public Advocate, if the nearest relative cannot be notified`

GIVEN `an s 54(3) event has happened` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the principal has capacity for the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is another attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is an alternative attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I am able to notify the nearest relative` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `Who must be told`
`s 54(3), (4) -- who must be told` `an s 54(3) event has happened` `the principal has capacity for the matter` `there is another attorney` `there is an alternative attorney` `I am able to notify the nearest relative` MEANS
    IF NOT `an s 54(3) event has happened`
    THEN EMPTY
    ELSE IF `the principal has capacity for the matter`
         THEN `the principal` FOLLOWED BY `the others`
         ELSE IF `there is another attorney` OR `there is an alternative attorney`
              THEN `the others`
              ELSE IF `I am able to notify the nearest relative`
                   THEN LIST `the principal's nearest relative`
                   ELSE LIST `the Public Advocate, if the nearest relative cannot be notified`
    WHERE
        `the others` MEANS
            IF `there is another attorney`
            THEN IF `there is an alternative attorney`
                 THEN LIST `every other attorney`, `every alternative attorney`
                 ELSE LIST `every other attorney`
            ELSE IF `there is an alternative attorney`
                 THEN LIST `every alternative attorney`
                 ELSE EMPTY

-- s 40(1): "Before an attorney ... for the first time commences to exercise power for a matter because the principal
-- does not have decision making capacity for that matter, the attorney must take reasonable steps to give notice ...
-- to any person who, the enduring power of attorney states, should be so notified." (2): failure "does not affect any
-- exercise by the attorney of power". Fork F7: where it is not the first time, or the power names no one, s 40 asks
-- nothing (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `I am about to act for the first time because the principal lacks capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power names people to notify` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 40 -- I must notify before acting` `I am about to act for the first time because the principal lacks capacity` `the power names people to notify` IF
    `I am about to act for the first time because the principal lacks capacity` AND `the power names people to notify`

§§ `Part 6 -- the attorney's dealings`

-- s 64(1): "An attorney for financial matters ... has a duty not to enter into a transaction in that capacity if the
-- transaction is one in which there is or may be a conflict between (a) the duty of the attorney to the principal; and
-- (b) the interests of the attorney, or a relative, business associate or close friend of the attorney." (2): not "(a)
-- a gift made in accordance with section 67; or (b) ... maintenance of a dependant ... in accordance with section 68;
-- or (c) ... merely because ... the attorney ... (i) deals with an interest in property held jointly by the attorney and
-- the principal ...; or (ii) obtains a loan or gives a guarantee or indemnity in respect of [(i)]; or (iii) acquires an
-- interest in property to be held jointly ..., when the principal has decision making capacity for the matter; or (iv)
-- [a loan or guarantee for (iii)], when the principal has decision making capacity". s 65: despite s 64, the attorney
-- may enter into a conflict transaction (1) the principal authorised beforehand, (4) VCAT authorised beforehand; may
-- continue an uncompleted one (2) the principal validates while having capacity; a completed one may be validated by
-- the principal while having capacity (3) or by VCAT (5); (6) "taken to be valid from its commencement". Fork F8: the
-- capacity in (2)(c)(iii), (iv) is the principal's capacity at the time of the transaction. s 64 binds only an attorney
-- for financial matters: for another attorney, not covered (NOTHING-kind; s 63(1)(d) still applies).
DECLARE `Exception the transaction falls under` IS ONE OF
    `no exception`
    `a gift made under s 67`
    `maintenance of my dependant under s 68`
    `dealing with property my attorney and I hold jointly, or a loan or guarantee for it`
    `acquiring property to be held jointly with my attorney, or a loan or guarantee for it`

DECLARE `Whether my attorney may enter into the transaction` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is not a conflict transaction (s 64(1))`
    `yes: s 64(2) takes it out of the duty`
    `yes: I authorised it beforehand (s 65(1))`
    `yes: VCAT authorised it beforehand (s 65(4))`
    `it stands: I validated it while I had capacity for it, and it is valid from its commencement (s 65(2), (3), (6))`
    `it stands: VCAT validated the completed transaction, and it is valid from its commencement (s 65(5), (6))`
    `no: a conflict transaction my attorney must not enter into without my or VCAT's authority (s 64(1))`
    `not covered: s 64 binds only an attorney for financial matters (s 63(1)(d) still applies)`

GIVEN `the attorney is for financial matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is or may be a conflict` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the exception` IS A `Exception the transaction falls under`
      `I had capacity for the matter at the time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I authorised it beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT authorised it beforehand` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is completed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I validated it while I had capacity` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT validated it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether my attorney may enter into the transaction`
`ss 64, 65 -- whether my attorney may enter into the transaction` `the attorney is for financial matters` `there is or may be a conflict` `the exception` `I had capacity for the matter at the time` `I authorised it beforehand` `VCAT authorised it beforehand` `the transaction is completed` `I validated it while I had capacity` `VCAT validated it` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the attorney is for financial matters`
            THEN `not covered: s 64 binds only an attorney for financial matters (s 63(1)(d) still applies)` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF NOT `there is or may be a conflict`
            THEN `yes: it is not a conflict transaction (s 64(1))`
        IF `excepted`
            THEN `yes: s 64(2) takes it out of the duty`
        IF `I authorised it beforehand`
            THEN `yes: I authorised it beforehand (s 65(1))`
        IF `VCAT authorised it beforehand`
            THEN `yes: VCAT authorised it beforehand (s 65(4))`
        IF `I validated it while I had capacity`
            THEN `it stands: I validated it while I had capacity for it, and it is valid from its commencement (s 65(2), (3), (6))`
        IF `VCAT validated it` AND `the transaction is completed`
            THEN `it stands: VCAT validated the completed transaction, and it is valid from its commencement (s 65(5), (6))`
        OTHERWISE `no: a conflict transaction my attorney must not enter into without my or VCAT's authority (s 64(1))`
    WHERE
        `excepted` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the exception`
            WHEN `no exception` THEN FALSE
            WHEN `acquiring property to be held jointly with my attorney, or a loan or guarantee for it` THEN `I had capacity for the matter at the time`
            OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 67(1): "Subject to any condition or restriction stated in an enduring power of attorney, an attorney for financial
-- matters ... may make a gift of the principal's property only if (a) the gift is reasonable having regard to all the
-- circumstances and, in particular, the principal's financial circumstances; and (b) the gift is (i) to a relative or a
-- close friend of the principal and is of a seasonal nature or for a special event; or (ii) a type of donation that the
-- principal made when the principal had decision making capacity ... or that the principal might reasonably be expected
-- to make." (2): it may be to the attorney or the attorney's relative, friend or connected organisation. "Only if": JUST
-- FALSE when a limb fails; a condition or restriction in the power that forbids it: JUST FALSE (fork F9). Not an
-- attorney for financial matters: outside the grant (NOTHING-kind).
GIVEN `the attorney is for financial matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power forbids or restricts this gift` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the gift is reasonable given my finances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is to my relative or close friend, seasonal or for a special event` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a type of donation I made, or might be expected to make` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 67(1) -- my attorney may make the gift` `the attorney is for financial matters` `the power forbids or restricts this gift` `the gift is reasonable given my finances` `it is to my relative or close friend, seasonal or for a special event` `it is a type of donation I made, or might be expected to make` MEANS
    IF NOT `the attorney is for financial matters`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 67 grants the power only to an attorney for financial matters
    ELSE IF (NOT `the power forbids or restricts this gift`)
            AND `the gift is reasonable given my finances`
            AND (`it is to my relative or close friend, seasonal or for a special event` OR `it is a type of donation I made, or might be expected to make`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 67(3): "An attorney must keep a written record of any gift by the attorney (a) that is made to (i) the attorney; or
-- (ii) a relative or close friend of the attorney; or (iii) an organisation with which the attorney has a connection;
-- and (b) the total value of which is of or over (i) the prescribed amount; or (ii) if an amount has not been
-- prescribed, $100." (4): the record sets out the amount and the recipient. The regulations are not deposited: the
-- prescribed amount is an input, 0 for none prescribed. s 66 separately requires accurate records of all financial
-- dealings, so a gift is always recorded in the accounts; s 67(3) asks for the written gift record.
GIVEN `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 67(3)(b) -- the gift record threshold` `the prescribed amount` MEANS
    IF `the prescribed amount` GREATER THAN 0 THEN `the prescribed amount` ELSE 100

GIVEN `the gift is to me, my relative or close friend, or an organisation I am connected with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total value` IS A NUMBER
      `the prescribed amount` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 67(3) -- I must keep a written record of the gift` `the gift is to me, my relative or close friend, or an organisation I am connected with` `the total value` `the prescribed amount` IF
    `the gift is to me, my relative or close friend, or an organisation I am connected with`
    AND `the total value` AT LEAST (`s 67(3)(b) -- the gift record threshold` `the prescribed amount`)

-- s 66: "An attorney ... must keep accurate records and accounts of (a) all dealings and transactions made for financial
-- matters; and (b) all material dealings and transactions made for personal matters." A personal dealing that is not
-- material is outside the duty's scope (no "only"): NOTHING.
GIVEN `the dealing is for a financial matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the dealing is material` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 66 -- I must keep records of the dealing` `the dealing is for a financial matter` `the dealing is material` MEANS
    IF `the dealing is for a financial matter` OR `the dealing is material`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 66(b) reaches only material personal dealings

-- s 68: "(1) ... an attorney for financial matters ... may provide from the principal's property for the needs of a
-- dependant of the principal, if the enduring power of attorney so provides. (2) Unless the enduring power of attorney
-- otherwise provides, a provision under subsection (1) must not be more than what is reasonable having regard to all
-- the circumstances and, in particular, the principal's financial circumstances." "If" and "must not ... unless": JUST
-- FALSE. Not for financial matters: NOTHING-kind.
GIVEN `the attorney is for financial matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power provides for maintaining dependants` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount is no more than reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power allows more than is reasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 68 -- the attorney may provide for the dependant` `the attorney is for financial matters` `the power provides for maintaining dependants` `the amount is no more than reasonable` `the power allows more than is reasonable` MEANS
    IF NOT `the attorney is for financial matters`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 68 grants the power only to an attorney for financial matters
    ELSE IF `the power provides for maintaining dependants` AND (`the amount is no more than reasonable` OR `the power allows more than is reasonable`)
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 69: "(1) An attorney for financial matters ... must keep the attorney's property separate from the principal's
-- property. (2) Subsection (1) does not apply to (a) property owned jointly by the principal and attorney; or (b)
-- property acquired jointly ... in place of property owned jointly". A flat "does not apply": JUST FALSE. Not for
-- financial matters: NOTHING-kind.
GIVEN `the attorney is for financial matters` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the property is owned jointly, or acquired jointly in place of joint property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 69 -- the attorney must keep the property separate` `the attorney is for financial matters` `the property is owned jointly, or acquired jointly in place of joint property` MEANS
    IF NOT `the attorney is for financial matters`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 69 binds only an attorney for financial matters
    ELSE IF `the property is owned jointly, or acquired jointly in place of joint property`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 70: "An attorney ... is not entitled to any remuneration unless it is specifically authorised by the enduring power
-- of attorney or by law." "Unless": JUST FALSE.
GIVEN `the power specifically authorises payment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the law authorises payment` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 70 -- the attorney is entitled to be paid` `the power specifically authorises payment` `the law authorises payment` IF
    `the power specifically authorises payment` OR `the law authorises payment`

-- s 71: where attorneys act severally and an attorney for personal matters and one for financial matters disagree on a
-- matter each may act on, "(a) either attorney may apply to VCAT ...; and (b) unless the enduring power of attorney
-- otherwise provides or unless otherwise ordered by VCAT, the decision of the attorney for personal matters prevails".
-- s 72: "(1) An attorney for financial matters ... must implement a decision of an attorney for personal matters ...
-- (2) Despite subsection (1), if the implementation ... would result in a serious depletion of the principal's
-- financial resources, the attorney for financial matters must apply to VCAT under Part 8 for an order".
DECLARE `What happens when my attorneys disagree` IS ONE OF
    `the personal matters attorney's decision prevails, and the financial matters attorney must implement it (ss 71(b), 72(1))`
    `the financial matters attorney must not implement it but must apply to VCAT, as it would seriously deplete my finances (s 72(2))`
    `as my power, or VCAT's order, provides (s 71(b))`

GIVEN `the attorneys act severally and each may act on the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power or VCAT provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `implementing it would seriously deplete my finances` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `What happens when my attorneys disagree`
`ss 71, 72 -- what happens when my attorneys disagree` `the attorneys act severally and each may act on the matter` `the power or VCAT provides otherwise` `implementing it would seriously deplete my finances` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `implementing it would seriously deplete my finances`
            THEN `the financial matters attorney must not implement it but must apply to VCAT, as it would seriously deplete my finances (s 72(2))`
        IF `the attorneys act severally and each may act on the matter` AND `the power or VCAT provides otherwise`
            THEN `as my power, or VCAT's order, provides (s 71(b))`
        OTHERWISE `the personal matters attorney's decision prevails, and the financial matters attorney must implement it (ss 71(b), 72(1))`

§§ `Part 6 -- protection, relief and compensation (ss 73-80)`

-- s 73: knowing includes "having reason to believe". s 74: if "the Supreme Court or VCAT considers that (a) an attorney
-- ... is or may be personally liable for a contravention ...; and (b) the attorney has acted honestly and reasonably and
-- ought fairly to be excused", it "may relieve the attorney from all or part" of the liability. s 75(1): an attorney who
-- acts "in good faith and without knowing that the power ... is invalid or has been revoked is entitled to rely on the
-- power of attorney as against the principal and any other person". s 76: one who "acts in compliance with any advice,
-- direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT is taken to have complied with this Act unless the attorney knowingly
-- gave the Court or VCAT false or misleading information".
-- s 77(1): "The Supreme Court or VCAT may order an attorney ... to compensate the principal for a loss caused by the
-- attorney contravening any provision of this Act relating to enduring powers of attorney when acting as attorney".
-- (2): even if (a) convicted, (b) the principal has died ("payable to the estate"), (c) the power is or was invalid or
-- revoked. (3): "This section does not apply if Division 3 applies." Fork F3: Division 3 is read to bar compensation
-- to the extent it protects or relieves (s 76 compliance, s 75 reliance in good faith, s 74 relief of all; s 74 relief
-- of part leaves the rest) -- read literally, any s 74 order, even for part, takes away all of s 77 (finding 2).
DECLARE `Relief from liability` IS ONE OF `no relief`, `relieved of part`, `relieved of all`

DECLARE `Whether I can be compensated` IS ONE OF
    `not covered: s 77 reaches only a loss caused by my attorney contravening the Act while acting as attorney`
    `no: my attorney acted on the advice, direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT and is taken to have complied (ss 76, 77(3))`
    `no: my attorney relied in good faith on a power not known to be invalid or revoked (ss 73, 75(1), 77(3))`
    `no: the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved my attorney of all of it (ss 74, 77(3))`
    `yes, but only for the part of the liability not relieved (ss 74, 77)`
    `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order compensation, payable to my estate (s 77(2)(b))`
    `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order my attorney to compensate me (s 77(1))`

GIVEN `the loss was caused by a contravention while acting as attorney` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my attorney acted on the advice, direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT without misleading it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the power was invalid or revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
      `my attorney acted in good faith without knowing or having reason to believe that` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the relief` IS A `Relief from liability`
      `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether I can be compensated`
`ss 73-77 -- whether I can be compensated` `the loss was caused by a contravention while acting as attorney` `my attorney acted on the advice, direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT without misleading it` `the power was invalid or revoked` `my attorney acted in good faith without knowing or having reason to believe that` `the relief` `I have died` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the loss was caused by a contravention while acting as attorney`
            THEN `not covered: s 77 reaches only a loss caused by my attorney contravening the Act while acting as attorney` -- NOTHING-kind
        IF `my attorney acted on the advice, direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT without misleading it`
            THEN `no: my attorney acted on the advice, direction or order of the Supreme Court or VCAT and is taken to have complied (ss 76, 77(3))`
        IF `the power was invalid or revoked` AND `my attorney acted in good faith without knowing or having reason to believe that`
            THEN `no: my attorney relied in good faith on a power not known to be invalid or revoked (ss 73, 75(1), 77(3))`
        IF `the relief` EQUALS `relieved of all`
            THEN `no: the Supreme Court or VCAT has relieved my attorney of all of it (ss 74, 77(3))`
        IF `the relief` EQUALS `relieved of part`
            THEN `yes, but only for the part of the liability not relieved (ss 74, 77)`
        IF `I have died`
            THEN `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order compensation, payable to my estate (s 77(2)(b))`
        OTHERWISE `yes: the Supreme Court or VCAT may order my attorney to compensate me (s 77(1))`

-- s 74, from the attorney's side: relief needs the court's view on both limbs. "If ... considers": JUST FALSE without.
GIVEN `I am or may be personally liable for a contravention` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court considers I acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 74 -- the court may relieve me` `I am or may be personally liable for a contravention` `the court considers I acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am or may be personally liable for a contravention`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 74 has nothing to relieve
    ELSE IF `the court considers I acted honestly and reasonably and ought fairly to be excused`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 78: "A person may apply for an order under section 77 if the person is (a) the principal; or (b) any attorney under
-- the enduring power of attorney; or (c) an executor or administrator of the principal's estate; or (d) the Public
-- Advocate; or (e) the nearest relative of the principal; or (f) any other person whom VCAT is satisfied has a special
-- interest in the affairs of the principal." "If the person is": JUST FALSE for anyone else (fork F10; the
-- Guardianship and Administration Act 2019 s 183 lists without "if", and that encoding answers NOTHING).
DECLARE `Who is applying` IS ONE OF
    `me, the principal`
    `an attorney under my power`
    `the executor or administrator of my estate`
    `the Public Advocate`
    `my nearest relative`
    `someone VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in my affairs`
    `someone else`

GIVEN `the applicant` IS A `Who is applying`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 78 -- this person may apply for compensation` `the applicant` IF
    NOT (`the applicant` EQUALS `someone else`)

-- s 122(1): "A person may apply to VCAT for an order under Division 2 ... if the person is (a) the principal; or (b)
-- ... any attorney ...; or (c) the Public Advocate; or (d) the nearest relative of the principal; or (e) any other
-- person whom VCAT is satisfied has a special interest in the affairs of the principal." The executor or administrator
-- of the estate is not in this list (finding 4): only under (e). "If": JUST FALSE otherwise.
GIVEN `the applicant` IS A `Who is applying`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 122 -- this person may apply to VCAT about my power` `the applicant` IF
    NOT (`the applicant` EQUALS `someone else` OR `the applicant` EQUALS `the executor or administrator of my estate`)

-- s 79(1): "An application for an order for compensation ... must be made (a) if the principal has died, within 6
-- months after that death; or (b) if the attorney has died, within 6 months after that death; or (c) if both ... have
-- died, within 6 months after the first death." (2): "The Supreme Court or VCAT may extend the time". While both live,
-- s 79 sets no time (NOTHING-kind; finding 3).
GIVEN `I have died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I died` IS A DATE
      `my attorney has died` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day they died` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 79(1) -- the day of the first death` `I have died` `the day I died` `my attorney has died` `the day they died` MEANS
    IF `I have died` AND `my attorney has died`
    THEN IF `the day` `the day I died` `is on or before` `the day they died` THEN JUST `the day I died` ELSE JUST `the day they died`
    ELSE IF `I have died`
         THEN JUST `the day I died`
         ELSE IF `my attorney has died`
              THEN JUST `the day they died`
              ELSE NOTHING

GIVEN `the first death` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the time has been extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 79 -- the last day to apply for compensation from` `the first death` `the time has been extended` `the extended last day` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind: s 79 sets no time limit while both are alive
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        IF `the time has been extended`
        THEN JUST `the extended last day`
        ELSE JUST (`the date` 6 `months after` d)

§§ `Part 8 -- VCAT`

-- s 117(1): VCAT "must not decide that an enduring power of attorney is valid, even though the requirements for
-- execution ... were not complied with, unless VCAT is satisfied that (a) the principal and attorney intended the
-- document to be an enduring power of attorney; and (b) at the time the document was signed, the principal had decision
-- making capacity in relation to the making ...; and (c) the principal (i) signed the document freely and voluntarily;
-- or (ii) freely and voluntarily directed the person who signed ... and was present". (2) the same for a revocation.
-- "Must not ... unless": JUST FALSE when a limb fails. Fork F11: when all are satisfied, JUST TRUE ("VCAT may").
GIVEN `VCAT is satisfied it was intended to have that effect` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied I had capacity when it was signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied I signed or directed the signing freely and voluntarily, and was present` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 117 -- VCAT may treat my defectively executed instrument as valid` `VCAT is satisfied it was intended to have that effect` `VCAT is satisfied I had capacity when it was signed` `VCAT is satisfied I signed or directed the signing freely and voluntarily, and was present` IF
    `VCAT is satisfied it was intended to have that effect`
    AND `VCAT is satisfied I had capacity when it was signed`
    AND `VCAT is satisfied I signed or directed the signing freely and voluntarily, and was present`

-- s 118: VCAT "must not make an order declaring that an enduring power of attorney is invalid unless VCAT is satisfied
-- that (a) the principal did not have decision making capacity ... at the time ... it was made; or (b) at the time ...
-- it did not comply with the requirements of the Act; or (c) dishonesty or undue influence was used on the principal to
-- make [it]; or (d) [it] was legally invalid when entered into." s 119: then "void from its commencement".
GIVEN `VCAT is satisfied I lacked capacity when I made it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied it did not comply with the Act when made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied dishonesty or undue influence was used on me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied it was otherwise legally invalid` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 118 -- VCAT may declare my power invalid` `VCAT is satisfied I lacked capacity when I made it` `VCAT is satisfied it did not comply with the Act when made` `VCAT is satisfied dishonesty or undue influence was used on me` `VCAT is satisfied it was otherwise legally invalid` IF
    `VCAT is satisfied I lacked capacity when I made it`
    OR `VCAT is satisfied it did not comply with the Act when made`
    OR `VCAT is satisfied dishonesty or undue influence was used on me`
    OR `VCAT is satisfied it was otherwise legally invalid`

-- s 120(2): "Before making an order under subsection (1)(b) to revoke the appointment of an attorney ... VCAT must be
-- satisfied that (a) the attorney is not complying with provisions of this Act ...; and (b) the principal does not have
-- decision making capacity in relation to making an enduring power of attorney giving the same power." JUST FALSE when
-- a limb fails. (1)(a) (revoking all or part of the power) carries no such condition (finding 5).
GIVEN `VCAT is satisfied my attorney is not complying with the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT is satisfied I lack capacity to make the same power` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 120(2) -- VCAT may revoke my attorney's appointment` `VCAT is satisfied my attorney is not complying with the Act` `VCAT is satisfied I lack capacity to make the same power` IF
    `VCAT is satisfied my attorney is not complying with the Act` AND `VCAT is satisfied I lack capacity to make the same power`

-- s 126: "A person is not entitled to apply for a rehearing ... if (a) the order at first instance was to suspend an
-- enduring power of attorney or a supportive attorney appointment; or (b) the order ... was made by VCAT constituted by
-- the President ...; or (c) the application was for a rehearing or leave". s 130(1): a person may apply "(a) if the
-- person was a party ...; or (b) if the person was given notice ... but was not a party ..., with the leave of VCAT;
-- or (c) if the person was not given notice ... and ... has a special interest in the affairs of the principal, with
-- the leave of VCAT; or (d) if the person is the Public Advocate, without the leave of VCAT." The principal and every
-- attorney are parties (s 124). "Not entitled ... if" and "may ... if": JUST FALSE outside.
DECLARE `The applicant's standing` IS ONE OF
    `a party to the first hearing`
    `given notice of the first hearing, but not a party`
    `not given notice, but with a special interest in my affairs`
    `the Public Advocate, as applicant`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `Whether a rehearing can be sought` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as a party, without leave (s 130(1)(a))`
    `yes, with VCAT's leave (s 130(1)(b) or (c))`
    `yes: the Public Advocate needs no leave (s 130(1)(d))`
    `no: there is no rehearing of this order (s 126)`
    `no: not a person who may apply (s 130(1))`

GIVEN `the standing` IS A `The applicant's standing`
      `the order suspended the power` IS A BOOLEAN
      `VCAT was constituted by the President` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application was itself for a rehearing or leave` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether a rehearing can be sought`
`ss 126, 130 -- whether a rehearing can be sought` `the standing` `the order suspended the power` `VCAT was constituted by the President` `the application was itself for a rehearing or leave` MEANS
    IF `the order suspended the power` OR `VCAT was constituted by the President` OR `the application was itself for a rehearing or leave`
    THEN `no: there is no rehearing of this order (s 126)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the standing`
         WHEN `a party to the first hearing` THEN `yes: as a party, without leave (s 130(1)(a))`
         WHEN `given notice of the first hearing, but not a party` THEN `yes, with VCAT's leave (s 130(1)(b) or (c))`
         WHEN `not given notice, but with a special interest in my affairs` THEN `yes, with VCAT's leave (s 130(1)(b) or (c))`
         WHEN `the Public Advocate, as applicant` THEN `yes: the Public Advocate needs no leave (s 130(1)(d))`
         OTHERWISE `no: not a person who may apply (s 130(1))`

-- s 133(2): "if VCAT gives oral reasons for making an order and a party then requests written reasons under section 117
-- of the VCAT Act, the day on which the written reasons are given to the party is taken to be the day of the order."
GIVEN `the day VCAT made the order` IS A DATE
      `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day written reasons were given` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 133(2) -- the day of the order` `the day VCAT made the order` `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` `the day written reasons were given` MEANS
    IF `written reasons were requested after oral reasons` THEN `the day written reasons were given` ELSE `the day VCAT made the order`

§§ `Part 9 -- offences (s 135)`

-- s 135: a person "must not dishonestly obtain" an enduring power of attorney (1) or its revocation (2), and an
-- attorney "must not dishonestly use" it (3), "to obtain financial advantage" or "to cause loss to the principal or
-- another person". Penalty: "In the case of a natural person, level 6 imprisonment (5 years maximum) or 600 penalty
-- units or both; In the case of a body corporate, 2400 penalty units." (4): invalid or revoked powers included. Penalty
-- units are not converted (the Monetary Units Act 2004 is not deposited).
DECLARE `Maximum penalty` HAS
    `penalty units` IS A NUMBER
    `years of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the offender is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Maximum penalty`
`s 135 -- the maximum penalty` `the offender is a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `the offender is a body corporate`
    THEN `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 2400, `years of imprisonment` IS 0
    ELSE `Maximum penalty` WITH `penalty units` IS 600, `years of imprisonment` IS 5

§§ `Deadlines run as regulative rules (ss 79, 133)`

-- Day 0 is the day the period runs from; WITHIN n allows the step on day n ("within n days after the day ...": the day
-- itself excluded, the n-th day after it the last day).
DECLARE `Deadline party` IS ONE OF `me, or the person applying for me`

DECLARE `Deadline step` IS ONE OF
    `apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply`
    `apply for an order for compensation`

-- s 133(1): "An application for a rehearing or for leave to apply for a rehearing must be made within 28 days after the
-- day of the order." No power to extend in this Act. The breach is the loss of the right, not a wrong.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 133 -- apply for a rehearing within 28 days` MEANS
    PARTY `me, or the person applying for me`
    DO `apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply`
    WITHIN 28
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `me, or the person applying for me` BECAUSE "no application for a rehearing or for leave within 28 days after the day of the order (s 133)"

-- s 79: the number of days allowed is worked from the dates (6 months after the first death, or the extended day).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
`s 79 -- apply for compensation within the time` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `me, or the person applying for me`
    DO `apply for an order for compensation`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `me, or the person applying for me` BECAUSE "no application for compensation within 6 months after the death, or the extended time (s 79)"

-- Runs a deadline rule by EVALTRACE: is the step, taken on day t, in time?
GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
      `the step` IS A `Deadline step`
      t IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `under` `the rule` `the step` `on day` t `is in time` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL t), (EVENT `me, or the person applying for me` `the step` t))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Where the step stands` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done yet, and still in time`
    `not done, and the time has passed`
    `done, but out of time`
    `no time limit under this provision`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Deadline party` `Deadline step`
      `the step` IS A `Deadline step`
      `the day time runs from` IS A DATE
      `it has been done` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was done` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`where the step stands under` `the rule` `the step` `the day time runs from` `it has been done` `the day it was done` `today` MEANS
    IF `it has been done`
    THEN IF `under` `the rule` `the step` `on day` (`the days from` `the day time runs from` `to` `the day it was done`) `is in time`
         THEN `done in time`
         ELSE `done, but out of time`
    ELSE IF `under` `the rule` `the step` `on day` (`the days from` `the day time runs from` `to` `today`) `is in time`
         THEN `not done yet, and still in time`
         ELSE `not done, and the time has passed`

GIVEN `the day of the order` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 133 -- where my rehearing application stands` `the day of the order` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` MEANS
    `where the step stands under` `s 133 -- apply for a rehearing within 28 days` `apply for a rehearing, or for leave to apply` `the day of the order` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today`

GIVEN `the first death` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `the time has been extended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the extended last day` IS A DATE
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE
      `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Where the step stands`
`s 79 -- where my compensation application stands` `the first death` `the time has been extended` `the extended last day` `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the first death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no time limit under this provision`
    WHEN JUST d THEN
        `where the step stands under` (`s 79 -- apply for compensation within the time` (`the days from` d `to` `the last day`)) `apply for an order for compensation` d `I have applied` `the day I applied` `today`
        WHERE
            `the last day` MEANS
                IF `the time has been extended`
                THEN `the extended last day`
                ELSE `the date` 6 `months after` d
